lmdb-js 3.5.3 data-v1 close leak (upstream defect in kriszyp/lmdb-js src/env.cpp)

Applied by setup_lmdb_v1.sh before node-gyp rebuild; the build fails if the
patch neither applies nor is already present (for example, after an lmdb bump).

EnvWrap::closeEnv() calls mdb_env_close() only for an env found in
envTracking->envs. Envs enter that list solely through checkExistingEnvs(),
which LMDB 0.9.90 invokes from mdb_env_open() via mdb_env_set_callback().
The LMDB_DATA_V1 build compiles LMDB 0.9.29, which has neither
MDB_OVERLAPPINGSYNC nor mdb_env_set_callback, so openEnv() never registers
its env and closeEnv() never closes it: each close leaks lock.mdb and two
data.mdb descriptors plus the data and lock-table mappings.

The patch registers the opened env when MDB_OVERLAPPINGSYNC is undefined, so
closeEnv() reaches mdb_env_close(). Remove it once lmdb-js ships a fix.

--- a/src/env.cpp
+++ b/src/env.cpp
@@ -394,7 +394,23 @@
 			pthread_mutex_unlock(envTracking->envsLock);
 			goto fail;
 		}
+	}
+#ifndef MDB_OVERLAPPINGSYNC
+	// LMDB 0.9.x (the LMDB_DATA_V1 build) has no mdb_env_set_callback, so
+	// checkExistingEnvs never runs and never adds this env to envTracking.
+	// closeEnv() only calls mdb_env_close() for tracked envs, so register the
+	// opened env here; otherwise every close leaks its fds, data map and lock map.
+	// 0.9.x cannot detect an env already open in this process, so nothing is shared.
+	{
+		SharedEnv envRef;
+		envRef.env = env;
+		envRef.dev = 0;
+		envRef.inode = 0;
+		envRef.count = 1;
+		envRef.hasWrites = false;
+		envTracking->envs.push_back(envRef);
 	}
+#endif
 	mdb_env_get_flags(env, (unsigned int*) &flags);
 	if ((jsFlags & DELETE_ON_CLOSE)
 	#ifdef MDB_OVERLAPPINGSYNC
